* test: synchronize orphan-pipe reader regressions on child exit [daveey]

* fix(tools): a deleted process cwd no longer crashes execute_code or the file tools [daveey]

A backend whose cwd was removed (worktree shipped or GC'd) failed every
execute_code call with 'dispatch error: [Errno 2]': _resolve_child_cwd
evaluated a bare os.getcwd() before its own staging-dir fallback. Add
agent.runtime_cwd.process_cwd() ("" on FileNotFoundError/PermissionError),
build terminal_tool_config._safe_getcwd on it, and route every tools/ cwd
consumer through it (code_execution_env, file_tools_paths, mcp_tool_config,
file_operations_search, process_registry, environments/local).

tests/tools/test_deleted_process_cwd.py: regressions for each path plus an
AST guard that fails on any new unguarded os.getcwd() under tools/.

* fix(kanban): comments record origin_gateway; wait-comment probe; refuse author-matching wake checks; wake_probe_stale [daveey]

A parked card's wake check counted comments WHERE author='macbook'; the Mac's reply arrived through the
example-hub relay as 'hub:gw:macbook', so t_01a17f81686694ec stayed parked 38 h after the answer
(self-heal desktop-00c4a3bda2).

- task_comments.origin_gateway (nullable, machine-local, back-filled from hub:gw:<x> / <x>/t_... authors);
  add_comment(origin_gateway=) / 'kanban comment --origin-gateway' (relay sender), default from the author
  spelling, else this gateway.
- 'hermes kanban wait-comment <task> --after-id N [--from-gateway X] [--contains T]': 0 match, 1 not yet,
  2 cannot tell; a gateway matches origin_gateway or any author spelling of it.
- Park guard (kanban_awaiting.resolve): a wake_check filtering task_comments by author (=, like, glob, in)
  is refused with code author_probe naming the wait-comment command; author != own still parks.
  Off switch: kanban.author_probe_guard: false. wake_check tool description says so.
- Detection: wake_probe_stale. A parked card whose reason/probe names a example-hub request whose owner card
  is done, while its probe still exits 1, wakes once with a dispatcher comment.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_comment_origin.py (16 red before, 19 green after).

* refactor(kanban): comment-id queries move to kanban_db_comment_ids; origin migration in kanban_comment_origin; narrow excepts [daveey]

Code-health offsets for the origin_gateway change: kanban_db.py stays under its line cap,
_migrate_add_optional_columns under CC 20, no blind excepts.

* fix(plugins): serve has_hook from a fingerprint-checked hook record so cold kanban assign skips plugin discovery [daveey]

assign_task -> notify_task_updated -> has_hook ran a full plugin discovery in every
cold gate helper (38-57s under macOS background QoS on the mini). Every discovery
now records the hook names its plugins handle (registered or manifest-declared),
stamped with the pre-sweep plugins_snapshot fingerprint, in cache/plugin_hooks.json.
has_hook on an undiscovered manager answers from that record while the fingerprint
matches; True still discovers in the invoke that follows. Missing, stale or corrupt
records, and sweeps in which a plugin load timed out, fall back to full discovery.

* test+docs: manifest-declared hook served True; hook-registration contract [daveey]

* test: synchronize orphan-pipe reader regressions on child exit [daveey]
